  what the fixes are worth (cumulative):
      192.8  (bw  25.69 GiB/s, md  1446.9 kIOPS)  as measured, valid 300 s run
      192.8  (bw  25.69 GiB/s, md  1446.9 kIOPS)  + one directory's entries spread over all MDTs (name hash), finer MDT locks (done: ROCEPOOL_DIR_STRIPE=1 + MD_BUCKETS; a no-op on a run that already has them)
      192.8  (bw  25.69 GiB/s, md  1446.9 kIOPS)  + FOPEN_PARALLEL_DIRECT_WRITES: no per-node inode lock on a shared file
      192.8  (bw  25.69 GiB/s, md  1446.9 kIOPS)  + FUSE over io_uring (per-core queues, Linux 6.14+): ~3x per-mount rate, less wake-up cost (implemented: io500_run.py probes it against /dev/fuse on the hosts and uses the faster; a no-op on a run that already used it)
      192.8  (bw  25.69 GiB/s, md  1446.9 kIOPS)  + the LD_PRELOAD interception library in every rank (no FUSE channel, no kernel on the I/O path; implemented: io500_run.py --client auto probes it against FUSE and uses the faster; a no-op on a run that already used it)
      192.8  (bw  25.69 GiB/s, md  1446.9 kIOPS)  + one-sided reads and lookups (client RDMA READs stripes and MDT entries; implemented: io500_run.py --direct-read auto probes it; a no-op on a run that already used it -- its effect is in the measured per-op server CPU)
